0.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="/_next/static/media/Boyrun-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=792405807634160&amp;ev=PageView&amp;noscript=1" as="image" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">{"@type":"Organization","@context":"https://schema.org","url":"https://www.meetup.com/find/","name":"Meetup","logo":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/general/m_redesign_630x630.png","sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/meetup/","https://twitter.com/Meetup/","https://www.youtube.com/meetup","https://www.instagram.com/meetup/"]}</script><title data-next-head="">Find Events &amp; Groups | Meetup</title><meta name="description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="fb:app_id" content="2403839689" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:type" content="article" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:title" content="Find Events &amp; Groups | Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:app_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:package" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:app_store_id" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:app_name" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:should_fallback" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Return of the Moral State: Philosophy and the Good Life","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316761865/","description":"Across the world, politics is returning to one of its oldest questions: should the state promote particular, substantive conceptions of the good life? Modern liberalism has approached this ambition with suspicion, seeking instead to leave individuals and communities free to pursue different visions of human flourishing. Yet from Hungary and the United States to China, India, and Israel, influential movements and governments increasingly reject this restraint, using law, education, welfare, media, and public culture to promote specific ideals of family, order, harmony, pride, sacrifice, and belonging.\n\nThis talk examines the return of what I call the “good life state.” I argue that these projects cannot be understood only through the languages of authoritarianism, populism, or democratic backsliding. They also offer substantive moral visions — sometimes attractive, sometimes dangerous — of how people ought to live. Their rise poses a difficult question for liberalism: how can it respond to rival visions of the good life without becoming a good life state itself?\n\nAlexandre Lefebvre\nhttps://profiles.sydney.edu.au/alex.lefebvre\nProfessor of Politics and Philosophy\nUniversity of Sydney\n\n**About the Speaker:**\n\nI’m Professor of Politics and Philosophy at the University of Sydney, where I explore how political ideas shape our lives. Originally from Vancouver, Canada, I earned my PhD at Johns Hopkins University in 2007 and now call Sydney home. For more than a decade, my work has explored one central idea: politics does not just govern us. Political ideas and institutions reach deep into our lives, forming who we are, what we value, and how we understand what makes a life worth living.\n\nMy latest book, **[Liberalism as a Way of Life](https://www.alexlefebvre.com/books)**, argues that liberalism deeply informs not just our politics, but also our values, humor, morality, and so much more. It was named a Best Book of 2024 by The New Yorker, Australian Book Review, Persuasion, and The Ministry of Pop Culture, and was praised as “stirring and clarifying” by David Brooks in *The New York Times* and “daring and engrossing” by Becca Rothfeld in *The Washington Post*.\n\nMy current project, *The Good Life State,* examines a global return to one of politics’ oldest ambitions: using state power to shape citizens’ conceptions of the good life.\n\n**\\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\***\n\nThis is a talk with audience Q&A presented by the University of Toronto's Centre for Ethics that is free to attend and open to the public. Free refreshments will be provided at the event. The talk will also be streamed online with live chat here [to be posted].\n\nAbout the Centre for Ethics (http://ethics.utoronto.ca):\n\nThe Centre for Ethics is an interdisciplinary centre aimed at advancing research and teaching in the field of ethics, broadly defined. The Centre seeks to bring together the theoretical and practical knowledge of diverse scholars, students, public servants and social leaders in order to increase understanding of the ethical dimensions of individual, social, and political life.\n\nIn pursuit of its interdisciplinary mission, the Centre fosters lines of inquiry such as (1) foundations of ethics, which encompasses the history of ethics and core concepts in the philosophical study of ethics; (2) ethics in action, which relates theory to practice in key domains of social life, including bioethics, business ethics, and ethics in the public sphere; and (3) ethics in translation, which draws upon the rich multiculturalism of the City of Toronto and addresses the ethics of multicultural societies, ethical discourse across religious and cultural boundaries, and the ethics of international society.\n\nThe Ethics of A.I. Lab at the Centre For Ethics recently appeared on a list of 10 organizations leading the way in ethical A.I.: https://ocean.sagepub.com/blog/10-organizations-leading-the-way-in-ethical-ai","startDate":"2026-10-08T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Larkin Building, Room 200","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"15 Devonshire Place, University of Toronto, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cafe Français au Black Pony - $3","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/events/316687657/","description":"(English below) Venez profiter de la bonne nourriture et d'une bonne conversation en français au café **Black Pony** situé au **1481 Gerrard St East.** Nous serons à l'arrière du café autour d'une grande table, prêts à vous accueillir.\n\nOn va pratiquer la langue de Molière tout en nous faisant de nouveaux amis(es)s. **Toutes les 30 minutes, nous changerons de place** pour favoriser les échanges. Tout le monde est bienvenu, quel que soit son niveau.\n\nPour en savoir plus sur le café et son menu délicieux et varié : [https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/](https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/)\n\nSi vous ne souhaitez pas que votre photo soit publiée sur MeetUp, veuillez en informer Vishnu.\n\n**Pourquoi ces frais de 3$?** C'est pour payer le coût de l'hébergement sur la plate-forme Meetup pour l’année courante et les années précédentes. Nous vous demandons de payer $3.00 à chaque événement. Vishnu sera là pour recueillir vos contributions. Nous vous prions de bien vouloir apporter de la monnaie.\n\nSi vous préférez, vous pouvez utiliser ce lien pour payer sur Square: [CLIQUER ICI](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nMerci,\n**Vishnu**\n\n..................................................................................................................\n\nCome and enjoy good food and good conversation at the **Black Pony café** located at **1481 Gerrard St East.** We'll be in the back of the café around a big table, ready to welcome you.\n\nWe'll be practicing the French language and making friends, **keeping in mind that every 45 minutes we'll be moving around to mix up the conversation.** Everyone is welcome, whatever your level.\n\nTo find out more about the cafe and its delicious and varied menu: https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/\n\nWhy the $3 fee? It helps cover the cost of hosting the group on the Meetup platform for the current year and previous years. We ask participants to contribute **$3.00 at each event**. Vishnu will be there to collect contributions, so please bring change.\n\nIf you prefer, you can use this Square link:\n[CLICK HERE](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nThank you,\nVishnu","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Black Pony Café and Snack Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1481 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🌙🍂 Fall Evening Walk: High Park & Ghost Stories 👻","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316200396/","description":"# 🌙🍂 **Fall Evening Walk: High Park & Ghost Stories** 👻\n\n### Fall Colours, Spooky Stories & A Different Way to Spend Your Evening\n\nLooking for something a little different to do after work?\n\nJoin us for an **evening walk through High Park**, where we'll enjoy the fall colours while stopping along the way for some of the park's stranger, spookier, and downright weird stories.\nHigh Park has a long history of ghost stories and local legends.\n\nFrom stories connected to the **War of 1812** — yes, *that* War of 1812 — to tales of mysterious deaths and people who may not have completely left the park behind, there's plenty of history to make an ordinary fall walk a little more interesting.\nBut don't worry.\n\n**This isn't a terrifying ghost hunt.** 👻\n\nThink **fall colours, creepy stories, a little history, a few laughs, and just enough spooky atmosphere to make you look over your shoulder once or twice.**\n\nIt's a relaxed way to get outside after work, explore one of Toronto's most beautiful parks, and experience High Park as the daylight starts to disappear. 🍂🌙\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll walk through **High Park**, stopping at different locations along the way while I share stories connected to the park's history and ghostly legends.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore some of High Park's most interesting locations\n* Hear stories of ghosts, legends, and strange events 👻\n* Learn a little about the park's history\n* Take photos and enjoy the scenery 📸\n* Have some Halloween fun along the way 🎃\n\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace, with regular stops for storytelling.\nThe walk will remain **outside throughout** — there is no entry into buildings.\n\n***\n\n## So Let's Have Some Fun\n\nThis isn't meant to be a serious paranormal investigation.\n\nSome stories are creepy. Some are strange. Some might make you wonder whether there's actually something going on.\nAnd some are just a good excuse to tell a spooky story while walking through the fall leaves.\n\n**You don't have to believe in ghosts.**\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nHigh Park can be cool and damp in late October, so bring a warm jacket and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll be walking at a steady pace, with stops along the way for stories and photos.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park sign on the west side at Bloor Street West & High Park Avenue\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶 **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** Back where we started\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated, guided storytelling experience**, rather than one of our regular group walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Warm fall jacket or layers\n📸 Camera or phone\n🎃 Halloween spirit\nAnd if you want to wear a costume...\n**I'm certainly not going to stop you.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* People who love Halloween 🎃\n* Anyone who enjoys ghost stories\n* Fall-colour enthusiasts 🍂\n* History buffs\n* People looking for something different to do on Halloween Day\n* Anyone who enjoys a good story and a few laughs\n* People who want to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the fall colours.** 🍂\n**Stay for the ghost stories.** 👻\n**Leave with a new connection — if the ghosts don't get you first.** 🎃","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"High Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Bloor and High Park Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"French at the Royal Conservatory","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/315915448/","description":"Join us for an evening of French conversation at B Espresso Bar in the atrium of the Toronto Royal Conservatory of Music (near St. George station)! We welcome all levels of French, and it's free\\*. Venez pratiquer votre français!\n\n\\*While there is no fee to attend this event, guests are expected to purchase something from B Espresso Bar, in accordance with RCM's restrictions on usage of the cafe atrium space.\n\n**Building location:**\nThe Royal Conservatory is at 273 Bloor St W, between Varsity Stadium and the Royal Ontario Museum (ROM). There are entrances off Bloor St. and Philosopher's Walk. If you enter from Bloor St through the large glass doors, follow the hallway on the left beside the staircase and turn left at the end. (Closest TTC: St. George)\n\n**Notes and restrictions:**\nThe host may or may not attend this event. Attendees are encouraged to seat themselves at two or more adjacent tables, as needed. Please form groups of 6 people at each table; do not rearrange chairs and tables to accommodate more people, as this obstructs the narrow walking space. Guests are expected to order something from the cafe, and are asked to please refrain from bringing outside food or drink. Attendees must leave the building at 8pm when the cafe stops serving.\n\n**Contributions:**\nIf you are a regular with us and would like to support the group, please send any contributions by e-transfer to [diskutomeetup@gmail.com.](http://diskutomeetup@gmail.com.) The yearly donation goal and amounts received year-to-date will be tracked anonymously on [this google sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18GfqYsis8Cf2XGg4KsKQJsY_0Fv3bsSQHwJAxvC1Km8/edit?usp=sharing). Thank you so much for your support.","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Royal Conservatory of Music","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🧠💡❓Trivia Night @ The Frog: A Firkin Pub","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316704196/","description":"## 🧠🎉 Trivia Night @ The Frog: A Firkin Pub 🍻\n\n**Think fast, laugh hard, and make new friends!**\nWe’ll be meeting at **The Frog: A Firkin Pub**, conveniently located just steps from **Yonge–Sheppard Station** — cozy - great food and fun!\n\n### 🕖 About the Event\n\nTrivia starts at **7:00 PM** and runs until around **9:30 P**M— just **ask for Colleen’s group** when you arrive!\n\nExpect a lively mix of **pop culture, history, music, sports, and random fun question.** Whether you come solo or bring a friend, we’ll make sure everyone’s part of a team. 🧩💬\n\n### 💸 Cost & Policy\n\nEveryone must spend at least **$10 (plus tax & tip)** at the pub.\n\n**NEW POLICY:**\n\n* 🆕 *First-timers* must send a **$5 deposit** by e-transfer to **tommills@rogers.com** and message Colleen right away on this page or the sign-up page. you'll be refunded in cashif/when you show up.\n* 💌 There will be a **$1 reminder charge** if you don’t send the deposit promptly, for each reminder.\n* 👥 You may bring **1 guest**, but please e-transfer **$10** in advance. You’ll be refunded once your guest arrives.\n\n### 🧠 Why You’ll Love It\n\nTrivia night isn’t just about questions — it’s about **connection, laughter, and teamwork**. Come test your wits, cheer on your tablemates, and enjoy the buzz of a pub full of friendly faces. Whether you’re a trivia pro or just in it for the fun, it’s always a great time!\n\n📱 **Don’t forget to join our WhatsApp group** – [CLICK HERE!](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc?mode=ac_t)\n\n### ⚠️ Notes\n\n* Please don’t just “show up” without RSVPing — seating is limited, and teams need to be balanced.\n* Occasionally, the organizer may need to rearrange teams if one is *too stacked* (e.g., all the sports or music experts together!).\n* Sometimes things happen — events can be canceled or adjusted, so keep an eye out for updates.\n\n📩 **Questions?**\nContact **Colleen**, your organizer, by posting on the event page.","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Frog: A Firkin Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4854 Yonge St, North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[CAS] ENG x MANDARIN Board Game Exchange (英语x普通桌游活动)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/events/316617315/","description":"*To join this event, you must be able to speak full sentences in Mandarin.\n\nThis event is for those wanting to practice Mandarin and/or English. Here, you can chat with others and play board games in either language to improve your linguistic skills. Feel free to join our WeChat group during the event, as it is the best way to stay connected with us.\n\nIf you have any questions, leave a comment on this event page.\n\n＜中文版＞\n此活动是以聊天和玩桌游练习中文或英文，等级不限，平时有6-10位参加者。此活动微信群可在活动中加入，互相学习，天天向上。\n\n如果您有任何疑问，请随时在活动页上留言或联系主持人","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"101 College St","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"101 College St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CAS Meetup Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/"},"performer":"CAS Meetup Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Toronto Comedy Showcase - Singles Night","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/events/316514645/","description":"**NOTE:** This is a ticketed event. You need a ticket to attend.\n\n**Tickets here:** https://comedybar.ca/shows/the-toronto-comedy-showcase-singles-night\n\nSingle and ready to mingle? We’re bringing together some of the city’s funniest comedians to share their most hilarious, cringe-worthy, and relatable stories about love, relationships, and the wild world of dating in Toronto.\n\nWhether you’re happily single, tragically single, or just looking for a great night out with friends, this is the show for you.\nExpect a night packed with sharp observations, wild dating app disasters, and plenty of crowd work.\n\nWho knows? You might even meet someone—or at least leave feeling a lot better about your own love life.\n\n7pm: Singles mix and mingle\n8pm: Show\n\nGrab your tickets, grab a drink, and get ready to laugh until it hurts. Because if we can’t find love, we can at least find the punchline!","startDate":"2026-10-08T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Comedy Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"945 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M6H 1L5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/"},"performer":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Startup Pitch & Networking in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-valley-toronto/events/316119379/","description":"📍 **Registration is on Luma — Meetup is not our RSVP platform.** Please register here to secure your spot: https://luma.com/f6r924dy\n\n🚀 **Join our event in Toronto!**\n\nWe design Pitch and Networking nights to help founders sharpen their thinking through direct, candid feedback and to give strong investors access to serious teams.\n\n**Our pitch night is complemented by a structured networking session before and after the pitch session.**\n\n▶ **See how our pitch nights look:** https://vimeo.com/877496618\n\n**💡 What to expect:**\n\n- **Startups pitch live and receive focused feedback** from angels and VC partners\n- **Structured networking session** before and after the pitches\n- Entrepreneurs, startup founders, and operators are joining to network, exchange ideas, and build strong connections\n- Active investors and venture scouts joining to discover the best startups early\n\n**🤝 Who you will meet at the event:**\n\n- Founders\n- Investors, VC partners, Venture Scouts\n- Marketers, Salespeople, Business Advisors\n- Industry Disruptors\n- AI Experts\n- Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia, and the United Kingdom\n\n**💼 We Welcome New Investors:**\n\nWe invite investors to our event to expand their network, get acquainted with new startups, evaluate them, share feedback, and participate in discussions with early-stage and serial founders.\n\nWe offer **complimentary tickets to institutional investors, angels, and venture scouts** with a proven track record.\n\nPlease [apply via Luma](https://luma.com/f6r924dy) or send us an email so we can issue the ticket.\n\nIf you'd like to **access our database of promising startups** or **provide mentorship support to our best startups**, please fill out this short [Investor Application Form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdn1s8f5_R3iaqYoJ4aU2q1IxcFXIZIQElD6cEcv8YkRQhaUA/viewform), and our team will contact you.\n\n**🎤 Want to Pitch?**\n\nA limited number of founders will have the opportunity to pitch their startup or business **to a panel of investors and experts.**\n\n4-6 selected founders will pitch their startup, followed by a short Q&A where participants can ask questions and share feedback.\n\nApply by filling out the [Pitch Application Form](https://forms.gle/CuscVQibyXBbi1Fv7) and sending us your pitch deck.\n\nSpots are limited, and we select founders in advance.\n\nTo maintain high-quality pitches, you are required to present with a pitch deck. We will share our **pitching guide** and, if you'd like, **coach you** so you're fully prepared for pitch night.\n\n🏆 **The best startups will be featured** across our social media and included in our **investor newsletter.**\n\n**Requirements for attendees:**\n\n- Dress code: smart casual. Bring good energy.\n\n**🎟 Join our event and secure your ticket today!**\n\n**About us:**\n\n[Startup Valley](https://startupvalley.club/) is a global event organizer hosting pitch nights in 25 cities since 2023. Since then, **we have hosted 850 events for 40,000 attendees**. Over these years, we connected countless outstanding early-stage startups to serious investors, and we are not planning to stop. We maintain strategic partnerships with VC funds in the US, Europe, and Asia to support our community.\n\nDo you have a **question, a partnership proposal, or want to clarify something**? Reach us at hello@startupvalley.club\n\n**Agenda**\n\n- 19:00–19:30 — **Registration**: Guests register, receive badges, and event programs. This is an opportunity for casual networking, making first connections, and preparing for the event.\n- 19:30–20:00 — **Event Kickoff & Interactive Networking**: Official welcome from the organizers with a brief overview of the event goals and schedule. Interactive networking session to connect with key contacts.\n- 20:00–20:50 — **Startup Pitch Session**: Startups present their projects to investors and experts. Each team has 5 minutes to pitch, covering the project’s core idea, business model, and target market.\n- 20:50–22:00 — **Chill & Networking**: Participants enjoy casual conversations with investors, discuss collaboration opportunities, and exchange ideas over refreshments.\n\n**FAQ**\n\n**Can I pitch?**\nYes! To pitch, please purchase a Pitch Ticket and fill out the Pitch Application Form. We will contact you to discuss and approve your pitch. The pitch duration is 5 minutes. You will also have some time to answer questions from the audience.\n\n**How does the pitch go?**\nSelected founders present on stage to the audience and the investors in the room. You get 5 minutes to pitch your idea, business model, target market, and investment ask, followed by a short Q&A. The best startups are featured across our social media channels and in the investor newsletter.\n\n**Who will I meet?**\nFounders, angel investors, VC partners, venture scouts, AI experts, engineers, operators, marketing and sales experts, and international entrepreneurs from across Europe, Asia, and the US.\n\n**Do investors get free tickets?**\nYes! Please apply via Luma (the link is in the event description) or email hello@startupvalley.club, and we will issue a complimentary ticket for you and your team.\n\n**Can I request a refund?**\nYes. Refunds are available if requested at least 1 day before the event start time. Please submit the refund request on the platform where you purchased your ticket, or email us at hello@startupvalley.club","startDate":"2026-10-08T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Kos Restaurant","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"61 Bellevue Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Startups & Tech Events in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-valley-toronto/"},"performer":"Startups & Tech Events in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ROTMAN Author Talk:  Power of Situations","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/314974584/","description":"We attend various ROTMAN events each year. Author Talks. Book Releases. Visiting Professors.\n\n### **Agenda:**\n\n5:00 pm - Check-in opens + light refreshments\n5:30 pm - Author presentation and moderated Q&A\n6:30 pm - Meet-and-greet with author + book signing\n\n### **Book Synopsis:**\n\n**From the #1 bestselling author of *Grit,* a new book that reveals the hidden power of situations—and how you can shape them to bring out your best.**\n\nAngela Duckworth, PhD, is the bestselling author of *Grit* and the founder and CEO of Character Lab. A 2013 MacArthur Fellow, she is a professor of psychology at the University of Pennsylvania.\n\n**In Angela Duckworth’s first book, she showed that a common denominator of successful strivers is a blend of passion and perseverance she dubbed “grit.**”\n\nTicket link is below. $22-$45\n\nThis second book springs from her deepening realization that grit, while necessary, is sometimes not sufficient. How you situate yourself to meet a challenge can be crucial.\nDuckworth’s in-depth research reveals the enormous influence wielded by the objects within arm’s reach, your peers and mentors, and even your zip code. Though you’re often told to make the best of your situation, it is far, far better to make your situation better first.\n\n**In *Situated*, you’ll discover:**\n\n* Why your personality changes, sometimes dramatically, from one situation to another—and how you can harness that shift\n* The secret to conquering temptation *without* willpower\n* Why taking the less effortful path can feel like cheating but often solves a stubborn problem\n* How the company you keep shapes the person you become\n* The most effective ways to help others succeed\n\n***TICKET Link here-***-\n\nhttps://www.rotman.utoronto.ca/news-events-and-ideas/public-events/events-listings/2026/october-2026/oct-8---angela-duckworth/","startDate":"2026-10-08T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"UofT Rotman School of Management","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"105 St George, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/"},"performer":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AWS 101 Workshop - Date TBD","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-seneca-polytechnic-newnham-campus/events/316658151/","description":"Welcome to the event where you stop watching and start building.\n\nAWS 101 is our first hands-on workshop, you're setting up your AWS account, getting into the console, and deploying an actual website to a live server before you leave the room. Not a simulation. Not a tutorial you follow at home. Something real, running on AWS infrastructure, with a URL you can send to people.\n\nWe'll walk through the core services that show up in almost every real architecture, (EC2, S3, IAM, RDS) breaking down not just what they are but why they exist and when you'd actually reach for one over another. That thinking is what separates someone who watched a YouTube video from someone who can answer an interview question.\n\nThen we put it all together. Teams of 2-3, a base project already set up, and a challenge to extend it with add-ons wire the database, upgrade the design, add a second page, set up a custom domain. First team to complete all four wins.\n\n**What to expect:**\nA Kahoot to kick off the hands-on section, a live guided build where everyone follows along, a team challenge with actual stakes, and a room full of people figuring things out together.\n**And yes — merch is dropping.** AWS SBG gear will be at this event for the first time. Winners of the challenge get first pick.\n\nFood's covered. Bring your laptop. Set up your AWS Free tier account now.\n\n**DATE TBD, expected early Octobe**r **· Helix Room, K Building, Newnham Campus**","startDate":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventS